{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/467093-a-few-forsaken-2nd-ed-questions","id":467093,"title":"A few Forsaken 2nd ed questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-03T00:49:14-07:00","id":467093,"title":"A few Forsaken 2nd ed questions","content":"I looked around but these didn't seem to be already answered anywhere. But I had a few questions about the new edition.<br /> <br /> Lunacy works differently now, and I've understood most of what they're talking about. What confused me was exactly <i>when</i> the Lunacy goes into effect. It says that the character suffers a breaking point, but &quot;...doesn\u2019t necessarily come immediately; it comes at the dramatically appropriate moment when the witness would otherwise take a rational breath and come to her senses.&quot; So does this mean, for instance, if the werewolf is fighting some gang members, and they all shoot him, then see his regeneration (or the werewolf goes gauru) they could quite possibly continue fighting until combat is done, then later on come to their senses and have a &quot;meltdown&quot;?<br /> It seems like they altered Lunacy to no longer be the &quot;humans run away and remember nothing&quot; win-button. Is that an accurate reading? (I mean I know gauru is still a win-button against most humans).<br /> <br /> &quot;Touching&quot; silver. on p 114 under the &quot;Facet modifiers&quot; you take a -3 to the activation of facets when you are &quot;in contact with silver.&quot; Does this require bare skin? Does holding a silver weapon count for this? Or is this more of a &quot;if someone puts you in silver manacles&quot; thing? Are there any other penalties or things associated with carrying silver or a silver weapon?<br /> <br /> Death rage triggers on p 103. The sidebar says &quot;Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him. Which trigger affects him at any given time depends on his Harmony.....Werewolves also have general triggers, events that will push any werewolf into Death Rage. All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; players can\u2019t pick and choose from them. &quot;<br /> So does this mean thatevery werewolf has two sets from that list? (General, and one other you pick) Or are you supposed to pick a number of them? If so, how many? Or do you have <i>all</i> of them on the list and you're supposed to make up one or two more for each individual? It seems to me that it's the first (so each character will have the general set and the other few that depends on her harmony) but I want to make sure.<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T03:19:37-07:00","id":467165,"title":"","content":"I'd say the &quot;dramatic moment&quot; could simply be any turn when the werewolf isn't actually attacking them. Say there's a bunch of people and the werewolf tears into one. His buddies are going to look at that, roll, and potentially lose their shit right there.<br /> <br /> Touching Silver: I would say it's bare flesh only, because there's nothing particularly mystical about that penalty. Touching silver just <i>fucking hurts</i>.<br /> <br /> Rage triggers: It was eventually established that the writers intent was that aside from general triggers each werewolf chooses <i>one</i> category of personal triggers, and reacts to each stage depending on harmony level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:15:56-07:00","id":469101,"title":"","content":"You could just as easily taken one from each though. My wife did and i decided not to argue the point with her. Besides that the ones she choose work out really well for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T20:36:23-07:00","id":469129,"title":"","content":"The lunacy question is a good one, especially considering &quot;Gaze of the Moon&quot;. I played it to take effect immediately when the target rolled, but I suppose maybe not? Anyone else got ideas on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:14:50-07:00","id":469151,"title":"","content":"I guess it makes sense for it to take place after a while. With Atavism, it says it only really comes into effect when you're confronted with the source of your lunacy or put into a stressful situation. With Delusion you have when confronting the werewolf or supernatural.<br /> <br /> Granted in a lot of situations these will be occurring instantly, like in your example where you're shooting the werewolf. I think, in that case, them shapeshifting into something large and scary might be considered a dramatic enough moment. But someone who was just watching the alley, then left might not have an issue with it until they start thinking about what they saw. If a werewolf was outright attacking someone, and that person managed to get away, I could see them not really being affected by the lunacy until they thought they were in a safe place and, again, started organizing their thoughts about what had just happened to them.<br /> <br /> And no, it's definitely not a 'humans run away' button. The Atavist condition would force them to make all-out attacks. The gang members might just, fueled by the bubbling primal fear inside them, decide that they need to keep emptying their bullets into that thing, then when they're empty use whatever else they have to attack it. The mind-altering is still there, though, only an Exceptional Success seems to allow the victim to remember how everything went down precisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T21:35:36-07:00","id":470868,"title":"","content":"So speaking of Atavism, would you allow someone with the condition to make ranged attacks? Technically all-out attacks can only be made with close combat weapons,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T01:47:51-07:00","id":471020,"title":"","content":"I would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T03:31:09-07:00","id":471067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/467093-a-few-forsaken-2nd-ed-questions?p=467165#post467165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage triggers: It was eventually established that the writers intent was that aside from general triggers each werewolf chooses <i>one</i> category of personal triggers, and reacts to each stage depending on harmony level.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound anything like what we understood in the writing/play testing stages. Do you have a reference for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T08:24:46-07:00","id":471227,"title":"","content":"That's what Chris said that Stew said: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457047#post457047\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...047#post457047</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:19:58-07:00","id":471600,"title":"","content":"Something that might want to be answered in a FAQ later.<br /> <br /> Skin Thief. If you use the skin of someone with Striking Looks, do you get Striking Looks?<br /> <br /> I know how I'm ruling it: totally. But I know some people don't like the idea of merits through player action. Also does anyone else think it could be a great use of the ability for a particularly hardcore werewolf to let their packmates skin 'enough' of them so that, one day, they could impersonate him to get them out of trouble or simply make it appear as if there were a half-dozen of him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:24:22-07:00","id":471606,"title":"","content":"It's temporary and you have to <i>murder someone and wear their skin</i> to use it, so yeah, I think that's an ok example of a merit earned in-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:59:27-07:00","id":471633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/467093-a-few-forsaken-2nd-ed-questions?p=471227#post471227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Chris said that Stew said: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457047#post457047\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...047#post457047</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that's Chris saying 'Stew said this but I prefer the other way', but doesn't link to Stew saying anything, and the way Chris prefers is the way I understood it to be - plus it's the way that's spelled out (IMO) very clearly in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:08:23-07:00","id":471671,"title":"","content":"It's not spelled out clearly, you can infer that where the book says pick one common, passive and specific trigger that it allows you to mix and match, but getting triggered by things that have no relation to each other makes absolutely no sense to me. Getting triggered by different degrees of the same thing makes much more sense to me. I believe it was back in the preview's comments sections was where Stew said pick one group of triggers but players could choose individual triggers if that's how you wanted to play. Stew left it up to the players to choose how they wanted to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\